<h2 id="privacy">Privacy Policy</h2>
<p>For SPILL &mdash; the conversation game</p>
<p>Effective date: 25 November 2026</p>
<p>SPILL is a conversation and party game. You pick a topic, read a prompt aloud, and talk. This policy explains, in plain English, what information SPILL does and does not handle when you play.</p>

<h3>In short: SPILL collects no personal information</h3>
<p>SPILL has no user accounts, no sign-in, no analytics, no advertising and no tracking. We do not collect, receive, sell or share your personal information, and we do not ask you to enter any personal information to play.</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Question</th><th>SPILL</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Do I need an account?</td><td>No. There is no sign-in.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Is personal information collected?</td><td>No.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Are my answers recorded?</td><td>No. Answers are spoken, never entered into SPILL.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Does SPILL track me?</td><td>No analytics, advertising or tracking.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Is anything stored?</td><td>Recently shown cards only, on your device only.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Is a game session saved?</td><td>No. Closing or reloading ends the session.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Who we are</h3>
<p>SPILL is provided by Maree Vazouras (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;). You can contact us about privacy at <a href="mailto:ophidiassecret@outlook.com">ophidiassecret@outlook.com</a>.</p>

<h3>Information we do not collect</h3>
<p>We do not collect any of the following through SPILL:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Names, email addresses, phone numbers or other contact details.</li>
  <li>Accounts, usernames, passwords or profile information.</li>
  <li>Anything you say while playing. Conversations happen between the people in the room and are not recorded, transcribed, uploaded or stored by SPILL.</li>
  <li>Location, contacts, photos, microphone or camera data.</li>
  <li>Payment information. SPILL does not take payments in the app, and there are no in-app purchases or subscriptions. If you buy SPILL from the App Store, Apple handles the payment and we do not receive your payment details.</li>
  <li>Usage analytics, advertising identifiers or behavioural tracking data.</li>
</ul>

<h3>What stays on your device</h3>
<p>To avoid showing you the same prompt again straight away, SPILL may keep a short record of recently shown cards on your device, inside the app or your browser&rsquo;s local storage. This record:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Stays local:</strong> stays on your device and is not sent to us or to anyone else;</li>
  <li><strong>Cards only:</strong> contains card identifiers only &mdash; not your name, your answers or anything about you;</li>
  <li><strong>You control it:</strong> can be removed by clearing the app&rsquo;s or browser&rsquo;s site data, or by uninstalling the app.</li>
</ul>
<p>SPILL does not save a game session. If you close or reload SPILL, your place in a deck is not saved and there is no history, favourites list or resume feature. That is by design.</p>

<h3>Website hosting and external links</h3>
<p>If you play SPILL on the web, the service that hosts the website may automatically keep standard technical server logs, such as an internet protocol (IP) address and browser type, as part of operating and securing the hosting service. We do not use those logs to identify or track players. If SPILL links to an external website, that website has its own privacy policy and we are not responsible for it.</p>

<h3>Children</h3>
<p>SPILL is a conversation game for older teens and adults. Some prompts, particularly in The Grey Area deck, discuss adult relationships and moral dilemmas. SPILL is not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone, including children.</p>

<h3>Security and retention</h3>
<p>Because SPILL does not collect or receive your personal information, we hold no database of player information to secure, retain or delete. The only record described above is the recent-cards record on your own device, under your control.</p>

<h3>Your rights in Australia</h3>
<p>Under Australian privacy law you have rights in relation to personal information held about you, including to ask what is held and to ask for a correction. Because SPILL does not collect or hold your personal information, there is ordinarily nothing for us to provide or correct. If you believe we do hold personal information about you, contact us at <a href="mailto:ophidiassecret@outlook.com">ophidiassecret@outlook.com</a> and we will respond.</p>

<h3>Changes to this policy</h3>
<p>If SPILL changes in a way that affects privacy &mdash; for example, if accounts, analytics or advertising are added &mdash; we will update this policy, change the effective date above, and publish the updated policy at the same link before the change takes effect.</p>

<h3>Contact us</h3>
