<h2 id="terms">Terms of Use</h2>
<p>For SPILL &mdash; the conversation game</p>
<p>Effective date: 25 November 2026</p>
<p>These terms apply when you download, access or play SPILL. By playing SPILL, you agree to them. If you do not agree, please do not use SPILL.</p>

<h3>About SPILL</h3>
<p>SPILL is a conversation game &mdash; &ldquo;Less small talk. More SPILL.&rdquo; It presents prompts from three decks &mdash; Food for Thought, Under the Surface and The Grey Area &mdash; plus &ldquo;Other Side&rdquo; follow-up prompts, a Mix It Up shuffle of the same decks, and closing questions in The Last Drop. There is no score, no winner and no account. SPILL does not save a game session, so closing or reloading the app ends that session.</p>

<h3>Who can use SPILL</h3>
<p>SPILL is intended for older teens and adults. Some prompts discuss adult relationships, infidelity, family conflict, money and other mature themes, in discussion form only. If you are under 18, use SPILL with the agreement of a parent or guardian and only with prompts that are appropriate for you and the people playing with you.</p>

<h3>Playing with others</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Anyone may pass on any prompt, at any time, for any reason. No one has to answer a prompt, explain a pass, or share anything they would prefer to keep private.</li>
  <li>Respect the room: What you choose to say while playing is your responsibility. Be respectful of the other people in the conversation, and do not use SPILL to harass, embarrass or pressure anyone.</li>
  <li>Your conversation stays yours: SPILL does not record or send your conversation anywhere. What is said in a game is between the players.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Not professional advice</h3>
<p>Every prompt in SPILL is a conversation starter for discussion and entertainment only. Prompts that touch on relationships, mental health, family, money, work or right and wrong are not counselling, therapy, medical, financial, legal or other professional advice, and playing SPILL is not a substitute for professional help. If a topic raised in a game affects you, please seek support from a qualified professional or a trusted support service.</p>

